From 3e862e339e32b457915f3af9c1f2e6694cad477f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordi Altayo <jordiag@kth.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:22:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add "Play on home audio" and "Queue on home audio" for
 yt-fifo

yt-fifo (https://github.com/jagjordi/yt-fifo) plays the audio of a video on
a Snapcast multi-room setup. Once its server URL is set in the video and
audio settings, the stream long-press menu and the Cast to TV picker get two
entries: "Play on home audio" interrupts what is playing there (POST /queue
with play_now), "Queue on home audio" appends to its queue. The request is
sent asynchronously and a toast reports the resolved title or the server's
error message. Playing from the Cast button pauses local playback, like a
cast does.

The Cast picker's fixed rows (TubeBeam, home audio) are now a list of
labelled actions instead of two hardcoded TubeBeam positions, and
FCastManager.hasTargets() decides whether the Cast button is shown.

yt-fifo is a plain-http LAN service, so the application declares
usesCleartextTraffic; Android 9+ blocks cleartext otherwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
